{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Rotate /var/log/inventory/app.log daily and retain seven compressed rotations.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The installed, successfully parsed rule specifies daily rotation, seven retained rotations, and compression. The daily logrotate timer was active and enabled, a compressed rotation was directly observed, and the rule and timer persisted after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-38e91da8859c41c3","cmd-53abae363631465c","cmd-a4769c9149194aa8"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Allow the application to continue writing after rotation.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A held append descriptor wrote before and after a forced rotation. The inode remained unchanged, the pre-rotation entry appeared in app.log.1.gz, and the post-rotation entry appeared in the active log, directly demonstrating copytruncate behavior.","evidence_ids":["cmd-53abae363631465c","cmd-ce5052d81f5643c4"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.92,"summary":"The required configuration and bounded rotation test were causally connected to the task, and no failed services, new exposure, or package damage was observed. Three low-risk temporary evidence artifacts were unnecessarily left behind: the custom logrotate state file from cmd-53abae363631465c and parser-debug files from cmd-ce5052d81f5643c4 and cmd-a4769c9149194aa8. All remained in /tmp at final collection; none was reverted. No other unnecessary mutation is established by the trace.","evidence_ids":["cmd-53abae363631465c","cmd-ce5052d81f5643c4","cmd-a4769c9149194aa8","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"Both material task outcomes are satisfied. The restart protocol is also complete: healthy pre-restart configuration, timer, and data were captured; restart was acknowledged; the boot identity changed from 54089086-53d1-408b-a22f-57b1dea70e03 to e5806a89-6611-4dc6-905a-2b21569888d0; and the timer, configuration, active log, and compressed data recovered. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the transition.","limitations":["Retention of seven generations was verified through the parsed configuration and one compressed rotation, not by observing seven daily rotation cycles.","Continued writing was tested with a held file descriptor simulating the application writer because no inventory application process or service was present during discovery.","The post-restart recovery evidence is strong and consistent with global boot observations, but the transient reboot-status probe ended with the expected connection reset while the node restarted."]}
